## Why This Is Asked
This tests the ability to design robust per-topic schema validation with proper error handling and reliable offset management in Kafka consumer applications.

## Key Concepts
- JSON schema validation with type checking for required fields
- Per-topic dead-letter queue (DLQ) implementation
- Offset commit semantics with at-least-once delivery guarantees
- Idempotent message publishing and canary testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function validateUserEvent(rawMessage) {
  try {
    const payload = JSON.parse(rawMessage);
    if (typeof payload.userId === 'string' && 
        typeof payload.signupDate === 'string' && 
        typeof payload.metadata === 'object') {
      return { valid: true, payload };
    }
  } catch (error) {
    // Parsing error
  }
  return { valid: false, error: 'Invalid user event schema' };
}
```

## Testing Approach
Deploy canary with mixed valid/invalid messages to validate schema enforcement, DLQ routing, and offset commit behavior before full rollout.

